<html><head><title>Learning activities</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><span style="font-family: Verdana;">Transdisciplinary education requires different learning activities and teaching methods than you might be used to.
Learning takes place through collaboration — with society, with other disciplines, and with yourself.
</span><p></p><p><span style="font-family: Verdana;">
To design this type of education, it’s important to understand how the learning process works. You can read more about this under the Theory tab.
</span></p><p><span style="font-family: Verdana;">
On the </span><b>Practice page</b><span style="font-family: Verdana;">, you’ll find an overview of useful learning activities and teaching methods. Let yourself be inspired and start experimenting.</span></p></body></html>